//? Title: Convolutional VAE: Spatial Inference Through a Gaussian Bottleneck
//? Subtitle: Average-pool and repeat adjoints, explicit noise and a code-only Bernoulli decoder
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
A spatial generative model must summarize an image without letting encoder feature maps bypass
its stochastic bottleneck. This convolutional VAE reduces pooled28×28 grayscale features to two
Gaussian coordinates, then decodes only the explicit sample through projection, nearest repetition
and convolution. A hand calculation checks pooling/repetition and their adjoints before the full
2,117-parameter model trains for96 Adam updates on statically thresholded MNIST. Four fixed
validation draws select epoch3. Heldout negative ELBO is209.11832 nats/image; decode(mu) MSE
is0.08569 versus0.08669 for the fitting-only pixel mean. The small improvement, blurred examples,
zero-code controls and unfiltered prior/grid outputs remain visible. Two latent coordinates and
short training do not establish useful generation, semantic separation or compression bitrate.
)
\toc

> A sampled code is the only bridge

The encoder uses same-padded3×3 ReLU convolutions1→8 and8→4, each followed by a
nonoverlapping2×2 average pool. The resulting7×7×4 map is flattened to196 features for
separate linear mean and log-variance heads, each of width2. The posterior is
q(z|x)=N(mu(x),diag(exp(l(x)))); explicit epsilon~N(0,I) gives
z=mu+exp(l/2)⊙epsilon. The decoder projects **only z** to196 ReLU values, reshapes7×7×4,
repeats each spatial value2×2, applies a4→8 ReLU convolution, repeats again and applies an
8→1 linear-logit convolution. There are no skips, deterministic spatial codes fed to the
decoder, transposed convolutions or labels. Exposed pool2 values are inspection endpoints.

[Kingma and Welling](https://arxiv.org/abs/1312.6114) derive the Gaussian pathwise estimator
and evidence bound. This small pooled/repeat-decoder architecture is an educational variant,
not a published benchmark configuration. The prior is fixed N(0,I), beta1, with no annealing.
For one explicit posterior draw per binary image,

$$
R_b=\sum_{j=1}^{784}[\operatorname{softplus}(a_{bj})-x_{bj}a_{bj}],\qquad
K_b=\frac12\sum_{d=1}^2[\mu_{bd}^2+e^{l_{bd}}-1-l_{bd}],\qquad
L=\frac1B\sum_b(R_b+K_b).
$$
\alttext(The Bernoulli reconstruction sums784 pixels, Gaussian KL sums two coordinates, and only images are averaged.)

Jensen's inequality gives log p(x)≥E_q[log p(x|z)]−KL(q||p); this objective estimates its
negative. It is not exact log likelihood or an importance-weighted bound. Sigmoid logits are
probabilities, not Bernoulli pixel draws. Decode(mu) is generally not E_q[decode(z)] because
the decoder is nonlinear. Summing pixels and latent coordinates is essential: averaging pixels
alone would multiply the relative KL strength by784.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/conv_vae_method.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
