\image(figures/conv_vae_hand.png)
// result_end

\caption(Left: original4×4 values divided by16. Middle: repeated block means. Right: the computed adjoint d(0.5||T(X)||²)/dX, divided by16 for the same display scale.)
\alttext(Three4×4 grids show the original row-wise ramp, its block means after repetition, and the identical analytic/autograd projection gradient.)

For stride-one same-padded cross-correlation, each shared kernel derivative sums all uses:

$$
\frac{\partial L}{\partial W_{uvco}}=
\sum_{b,h,w}X^{\rm pad}_{b,h+u,w+v,c}\,G_{bhwo}.
$$
\alttext(A convolution filter derivative sums products of padded input windows and output adjoints over all images and spatial locations.)

ReLU multiplies by its positive-preactivation mask; its derivative at zero is zero here. The
Bernoulli-logit derivative is(sigmoid(a)−x)/B because pixels are summed. At the Gaussian sample,
reconstruction contributes dL/dmu=dL/dz and dL/dl=0.5(dL/dz)⊙sigma⊙epsilon;
KL adds mu/B and0.5(exp(l)−1)/B. The optional independent oracle checks both initial and
selected-state kernel, dense-head, projection and bias derivatives with all these reductions.

> Executed architecture and unique parameter census

The seven learned layers have14 tensors and2,117 scalars: encoder1 80; encoder2 292;
mean394; log variance394; decoder projection588; decoder1 296; decoder2 73.
ReLU convolutions use [He initialization](https://arxiv.org/abs/1502.01852); dense heads,
the **ReLU dense projection** and output convolution use ordinary Glorot uniform. All biases
are zero. In particular, changing the projection initializer would change the original run.
The six decoder tensors alone hold957 scalars, independent of the encoder's values.

For plotting only, a786-entry shape probe packs784 pixels and two epsilon slots. Actual model
calls take NHWC image and epsilon separately. Named boundaries preserve both Gaussian heads,
the supplied-noise branch, KL and reconstruction. Decoder projection/repetition begins at z;
no pool2→decoder edge is introduced. Shared linear drawing scales retain a two-pixel minimum,
six sampled planes and eight sampled neurons. Repeated appearances of encoder dependencies
beneath the heads do not add learned scalars to the unique census.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/conv_vae_architecture.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  n::ParameterStore p(2011);
  n::Module         model(
      [&](const n::Tensor& packed) {
        auto image   = n::reshape(n::slice_axis(packed, 1, 0, 784), {1, 28, 28, 1}),
             epsilon = n::slice_axis(packed, 1, 784, 786);
        n::model_stage("Image NHWC", packed, image);
        n::model_stage("Supplied Gaussian epsilon", packed, epsilon);
        const auto o = n::models::ConvolutionalVariationalAutoencoder(p, image, epsilon);
        n::model_stage("Conv3 same 1 to8 / ReLU", image, o.conv1);
        n::model_stage("Average pool2", o.conv1, o.pool1);
        n::model_stage("Conv3 same 8 to4 / ReLU", o.pool1, o.conv2);
        n::model_stage("Average pool2 / inspection only", o.conv2, o.pool2);
        n::model_stage("Gaussian mean /196 to2", o.pool2, o.mu);
        n::model_stage("Gaussian log variance /196 to2", o.pool2, o.log_variance);
        n::model_stage(
            "Pathwise Gaussian sample", std::vector<n::Tensor>{o.mu, o.log_variance, epsilon}, o.z);
        n::model_stage("Sample-only dense projection / reshape", o.z, o.decoder_base);
        n::model_stage("Repeat2 / conv4 to8 / ReLU", o.decoder_base, o.decoder1);
        n::model_stage("Repeat2 / conv8 to1 / logits", o.decoder1, o.spatial_logits);
        n::model_stage(
            "Summed pixel NLL",
            std::vector<n::Tensor>{image, o.spatial_logits},
            o.reconstruction_nll);
        n::model_stage("Summed Gaussian KL", std::vector<n::Tensor>{o.mu, o.log_variance}, o.kl);
        n::model_stage("Mean NLL + KL", std::vector<n::Tensor>{o.reconstruction_nll, o.kl}, o.loss);
        return o.loss;
      },
      "Convolutional Gaussian VAE / sample-only bridge");
  n::ModelPlotOptions options;
  options.style                 = n::ModelPlotStyle::Graph;
  options.detail                = n::ModelPlotDetail::Blocks;
  options.max_neurons           = 8;
  options.sizing.spatial_scale  = n::ModelPlotScale::Linear;
  options.sizing.channel_scale  = n::ModelPlotScale::Linear;
  options.sizing.minimum_extent = 2;
  options.sizing.max_planes     = 6;
  const auto figure             = model.plot(n::zeros({1, 786}), options);
  if (p.count() != 2117 || p.size() != 14 || figure.parameter_count() != 2117)
    return 1;
  figure.save_svg("build/conv_vae_architecture.svg");
  std::print("14 leaves /{} unique scalars; no spatial decoder bypass.\n", p.count());
}
```
