> Selected metrics and weak reconstruction controls

Epoch3 test NLL is205.425587 nats/image, KL3.692729 and negative ELBO209.118317.
Decode(mu) pixel MSE is0.085688548 versus0.086689513 for the fitting-only binary pixel mean:
a small improvement in this short single-seed run. No test value or digit label selected the
epoch. The original heldout score before training was535.095112, but epoch zero was ineligible.

The gallery takes the first heldout record per digit0–9, without quality filtering. Rows are
binary input, decode(mu), posterior draw0 probabilities, draw1 probabilities, fitting pixel mean,
absolute decode(mu) error and zero-code decoder probabilities. All use fixed[0,1]gray, nearest
scale3 and gap4; errors are not amplified. Zero-code outputs include learned decoder biases;
they are a target-free control, not the prior predictive mean. Four posterior draws per split
are stored individually rather than mislabeled as a predictive mean.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/conv_vae_learning.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  std::ifstream f("build/conv_vae/history.tsv");
  std::string   line;
  std::getline(f, line);
  std::vector<double> epochs, nll, total;
  while (std::getline(f, line)) {
    std::istringstream r(line);
    double             e, train, a, b, c;
    r >> e >> train >> a >> b >> c;
    epochs.push_back(e);
    nll.push_back(a);
    total.push_back(c);
  }
  auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  p.lines(epochs, nll, "NLL", {37, 99, 235}, 2)
      .lines(epochs, total, "NLL + KL", {220, 38, 38}, 2)
      .title("Fixed four-draw validation / completed epochs only")
      .x_label("completed epoch")
      .y_label("nats per image")
      .save_svg("build/conv_vae_learning.svg");
}
