> Inspecting the seven spatial stages

The stage archive records the first eight heldout images with fixed draw0 noise. The figure
shows the **first** of those records. Rows are conv1,pool1,conv2,pool2,decoder base,decoder1
and final sigmoid probabilities. The first six rows share one display maximum per stage over
all eight records/channels; this is a feature-inspection scale, not a pixel probability scale.
Each channel is nearest-repeated to28×28 for comparison. Missing channel slots are gray.
The final row uses sigmoid of spatial logits on fixed[0,1], with no feature normalization.
Pool2 and decoder-base rows differ: one comes from the image, the other from sampled z only.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/conv_vae_stages.png", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  std::map<std::string, n::Tensor> a;
  for (const auto& [k, v] : n::load_npz("build/conv_vae/stages.npz"))
    a.emplace(k, v);
  std::vector<n::Tensor> tiles;
  for (int stage = 0; stage < 7; ++stage) {
    auto t = a.at("stage" + std::to_string(stage));
    if (stage == 6)
      t = n::sigmoid(t);
    else {
      const double maximum = n::max(t).item();
      if (maximum > 0)
        t = t / maximum;
    }
    for (int c = 0; c < 8; ++c) {
      if (c >= t.size(3)) {
        tiles.push_back(n::full({1, 28, 28, 1}, 220. / 255));
        continue;
      }
      auto channel = n::slice_axis(n::take_rows(t, {0}), 3, c, c + 1);
      if (t.size(1) != 28)
        channel = n::upsample_nearest(channel, 28 / t.size(1));
      tiles.push_back(channel);
    }
  }
  n::save_image_grid(n::concat(tiles, 0), "build/conv_vae_stages.png", 8, 0, 1, 4, 220. / 255, 3);
}
