> Reuse and evidence

The core models::ConvolutionalVariationalAutoencoder and ConvolutionalVaeDecode expose
owning Gaussian/spatial endpoints, including decoder-only intermediate values. Their input
checks cover dtype/range, NHWC shape, multiples-of-four geometry, explicit noise and matching
batches before leaf creation. Python/R call the same C++ model mathematics; the report owns
the complete editable training loop and all96 updates, with no legacy helper dependency.

All19 original archives, the exact batch TSV and complete training/validation history are
compared by dtype, shape and value bytes. Artifacts retain all seven stages, the initial and
selected-state gradients, first update, every epoch, selected weights, fixed/training noise,
all posterior/prior/grid predictions and zero-code controls. Independent NumPy checks both
sets of2,117 chain-rule derivatives, the exact Float32 first Adam step, spatial adjoints,
Gaussian banks and complete forward outputs. Fixed-noise repeats, changed-noise samples,
zero-epsilon means, target-free sampled decoding, single/batch parity and immutable inference
are executed checks. A finite three-epoch trajectory supports those results, not convergence,
semantic disentanglement, exact likelihood superiority or quantized compression claims.
